<Project>
  <!-- LOCAL override for building the tests standalone (outside the Rhino source tree).

       Both test projects target net48;net10.0-windows. The net10.0-windows tests build and
       discover fine, but the test host crashes on run against Rhino.Testing 9.0.5-beta /
       Rhino 9 WIP:

           The active test run was aborted. Reason: Test host process crashed

       In the IDE that means Test Explorer lists the net10 duplicates alongside the net48 ones,
       and running one produces a build log with no test results. Narrow the standalone build to
       net48, which runs green in VS 2026 Test Explorer, vstest.console and `dotnet test`.

       This must live in a .targets file, not .props: TargetFrameworks is assigned in the csproj
       body, and .targets is imported after it.

       The in-Rhino build ('$(InRhino)' == 'True') is deliberately untouched. Drop the net48
       narrowing once Rhino.Testing can host the tests on .NET 10. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(InRhino)' != 'True'">
    <TargetFrameworks>net48</TargetFrameworks>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
